<title>BELGIUM: Fischler says rice deal must stay.</title>
<headline>Fischler says rice deal must stay.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler told agriculture ministers on Tuesday that he rejected a Spanish call for a faster introduction of rice sector reforms than the current planned three years, an EU official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The effect would be to lower prices and increase aid and the Commissioner refused the request,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>Fischler also rejected an Italian request that the Council should take over troubled negotiations with the United States on a tariff cumulative recovery system for rice imports.</p>
<p>He told ministers that the threat of a complaint to the World Trade Organisation in Geneva (WTO) continues and he said that taking the negotiations away from the ceareals management committee would not help the negotiations.</p>
</text>
